        ("I back onto the golf course. Why do I get rats every winter?", "Because the course and its wetland are a year-round food and water source, and a tiled 1970s roof is a warm, dry place to breed when the nights cool. The fix is proofing the roofline and eaves on the course side, then secured bait stations placed where the rats actually travel, checked and documented. <a href=\"/rodent-control-perth\">Rodent management</a>."),
