        "Princess Wallington Reserve is the heart of the suburb, with its aquatic centre, soccer fields and a bushwalk area of mature tuarts and grass trees, and the City of Stirling is expanding it into a larger community parkland. Wanneroo Road on the west, Reid Highway on the south, Beach Road on the north and Mirrabooka Avenue on the east box the suburb in, and the reserves and road verges between carry rodents, native cockroaches and spiders from one street to the next. We adjust for the mix: on an original home the roof void and timber framing get close attention; on a new infill dwelling we check slab edges, penetrations and the neighbour's side of the fence, and we keep internal treatments low-odour and non-staining.",
