    pests=[
        ("Termites", "New homes beside retained bush, builder-installed systems bridged by paving and patios, slab penetrations under kitchens and bathrooms. Inspections to AS 4349.3 and management systems to AS 3660.2 that reinstate a continuous treated zone. <a href=\"/termite-inspection-perth\">Termite inspection</a>."),
        ("Coastal brown ants", "Warm dune sand under new paving, small lots and shared fences mean one super-colony across half a street. <a href=\"/ant-control-perth\">Colony-level treatment</a> with slow-acting non-repellent product and bait, never a repellent spray."),
        ("Rats and mice", "Neerabup National Park and the retained bush through Trinity supply them; new estates with unscreened eaves, roller-door gaps and open alfresco ceilings let them in. <a href=\"/rodent-control-perth\">Rodent management</a>."),
        ("Spiders and cockroaches", "Redbacks in retic boxes and under new limestone retaining walls, black house spiders on rendered walls, native bush cockroaches wandering in from the reserves on warm nights. <a href=\"/general-pest-control-perth\">General pest treatment</a>."),
    ],
    now="Spring in Alkimos: coastal brown ants are the first call as the paving warms along the new streets, followed by redbacks in the retic boxes and under the outdoor furniture. Rodents from the bush edge are breeding and looking for roof space. Homes from the first wave of Alkimos Beach are now old enough for a termite inspection to AS 4349.3 to be worthwhile before the November swarm, especially where paving has gone in since handover.",
    neighbours=["Butler", "Yanchep", "Quinns Rocks"],
